From c1c2fa105b249195f92368e24d6bb221522d423f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:56:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 035/118] include: podkop_slim keeps podkop's protocols,
 podkop_full adds every outbound

podkop writes the inbounds tproxy, direct and mixed, the outbounds direct,
socks, shadowsocks, trojan, vless, hysteria2, selector and urltest, the DNS
servers udp, tls, https and fakeip, and no services; any other outbound
reaches sing-box only as raw JSON. With the tag podkop_slim the registries
keep that, the tuic outbound and the local, hosts and mDNS DNS servers;
with podkop_full they also keep every other outbound: http, snell (1.14),
vmess, naive (with with_naive_outbound), tor, ssh, shadowtls, anytls and
hysteria. The types left out are registered as stubs, so a configuration
naming one fails with "... is not included in this build (podkop_slim)",
for the outbounds "..., install podkop-engine-full or rebuild with -tags
podkop_full". Without the tags the registries are upstream's.
